# OpenSpec workflow

This project uses [OpenSpec](https://openspec.dev) for spec-driven development.

## Before building a feature

1. **Propose first** — Run `/opsx-propose "<change-name>"` or ask the agent to create a change under `openspec/changes/<name>/`.
2. **Review artifacts** — Read `proposal.md`, `specs/**/spec.md`, `design.md`, and `tasks.md` before writing code.
3. **Apply in chunks** — Run `/opsx-apply` (or ask to apply the change) and complete tasks in order; mark `- [x]` in `tasks.md` as you go.
4. **Archive when done** — Run `/opsx-archive` to merge specs into `openspec/specs/` and archive the change.

## Rules

- Do **not** skip specs for user-facing behavior changes.
- Keep specs testable (WHEN/THEN scenarios).
- Implementation details belong in `design.md`, not spec files.
- One change per feature; small, reviewable task chunks.
- After apply, restart dev servers per `restart-dev-servers.mdc`.

## Active changes

Check `openspec/changes/` for in-progress work before starting overlapping features.
